---
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
---

<ContentPage
  title="Service Level Agreement (SLA) — FunctionFly"
  description="FunctionFly service level agreement (if applicable to your plan or order form)."
  contentWidth="wide"
>
  <div class="legal-header">
    <div class="legal-header-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
        <path d="M3 12h18"></path>
        <path d="M12 3v18"></path>
        <path d="M7 7h10v10H7z"></path>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <h1>Service Level Agreement (SLA)</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: March 24, 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="legal-card">
    <p>
      This page describes the Service Level Agreement (SLA) for FunctionFly where applicable. Not all plans include an SLA.
      If you have an enterprise plan, the SLA may be provided in your order form or a separate written agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability commitments</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Coming soon. If you need an SLA now, please contact us and we&apos;ll provide the applicable terms for your plan.
    </p>

    <h2>Service credits and remedies</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Coming soon. Remedies, if any, are limited to those expressly stated in the applicable SLA or order form.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For SLA questions, contact <a href="mailto:sales@functionfly.com">sales@functionfly.com</a> or
      <a href="mailto:legal@functionfly.com">legal@functionfly.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentPage>

